{"ts":"2026-09-25T21:16:21.435Z","author":"agent.claude.test-pilot","name":"messages/assistant/00000005","body":"All six steps ran. The child (`child-1`) is still running, so its result isn't in yet. I did not wait for it.\n\n**Onboarding**\n- I listed `origins/` (24 entries). I then read `origins/onboarding_1.12.md` with `fs_read`. It came back as one call covering all 262 lines, and `next_line` was null. [checked: tool output]\n\n**Step 1: draft**\n- `pilot/draft` was written with body `print('draft')` and tag `pilot.note`. Its ID is `20260925T211547Z:92`.\n- `fs_write` exported that body to `workspace:/smoke-draft.py`. It reported 14 bytes. The resolved path was `bootstrap-harness/gpt-anthropic-harness/task-5-subagent/workspace/chat-20260925t211547z-c353f7e485/smoke-draft.py`.\n\n**Step 2: safe script**\n- `python_execute` on `scripts:/safe_test.py` returned exit_code 0, status completed, not timed out and not truncated.\n- The output is in `pilot/script-output` (`20260925T211547Z:161`), authored by `harness`. It has the tags `execution.output`, `output.finished` and `output.reserved`.\n- I read its body with `ledger_read`: `safe_test diagnostic: completed` and `{\"script\": \"safe_test\", \"sum\": 42, \"filesystem_writes\": false}`. [checked]\n\n**Step 3: expected refusal**\n- `python_execute` on `workspace:/smoke-draft.py` with output_name `pilot/denied-output` was refused. The code was `capability_denied`. The message was \"Outside fs.execute bounds: …/smoke-draft.py; held: ['scripts:/safe_test.py']\". [checked]\n- This matches the expected bounds refusal, and I continued.\n- I did not check whether `pilot/denied-output` was reserved anyway. That is open.\n\n**Step 4: instructions**\n- `pilot/instructions` was written as `20260925T211547Z:112`. It has the Bar line and the text you gave, and the tag is `pilot.note`.\n\n**Step 5: child**\n- I started a haiku child with `instructions_id` `20260925T211547Z:112`, `result_name` `pilot/child-result` and exactly your bounds.\n- The harness returned `agent_id` `child-1`, author `agent.claude.child-1`, and status `running`.\n\n**Step 6: add and status**\n- `add(20, 22)` returned 42. [checked]\n- `subagent_status` with `wait_seconds` 0 showed `child-1` still `running`, with result null and error null. [checked]\n\n**Not verified**\n- **Result routing:** I haven't seen whether the child writes `pilot/child/report` or whether the harness records `pilot/child-result`.\n- **Child refusal:** I haven't seen whether the child's `fs_read` on `bootstrap-harness/rules.md` is refused.\n- **Result_name readability:** You said the result_name must be readable by both of us. My bounds cover `**` for reads. The child's `pilot/**` read grant covers it. I did not check this further.\n- **Child's `add` and `fs_read` calls:** Your bounds don't restrict tools. Whether it can call `add` at all is up to the harness.\n\nI initiated no further tests."}
