dence.\\n\\n2. **Arithmetic Test** [checked]: `add(19, 23)` returned `42` ✓\\n\\n3. **Bounds Test** [checked]: `fs_read` on `bootstrap-harness/rules.md` correctly refused with `capability_denied`. My grant-set restricts read access to `origins/**` only.\\n\\n4. **Report Written** [checked]: `pilot/child/report` (ID: 20260925T211547Z:493) recorded in ledger with `pilot.note` tag. Findings documented with claim labels and institutional context noted.\\n\\n**Observation**: Bounds enforcement is functioning correctly. Subprojects retain independent governance; I cannot access `bootstrap-harness/rules.md` as intended. Onboarding clearly states this architecture is by design.\\n\\n**Ready for direction.**\"}"}],"is_error":null}],"uuid":"80e594c8-7435-415a-91e4-4debd991495b","parent_tool_use_id":null,"tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"name\": \"pilot/child-result\", \"id\": \"20260925T211547Z:540\", \"author\": \"agent.claude.child-1\", \"prev\": \"20260925T211547Z:236\", \"tags\": [\"agent.result\", \"output.finished\", \"output.reserved\"], \"body\": \"I'll work through this systematically. Let me start by listing origins.\\n\\nNow let me read the required onboarding file completely:\\n\\nLet me continue reading the rest of the onboarding file:\\n\\nGood. I have now read the complete onboarding file (262 lines). Key institutional guidance noted:\\n\\n- Bar: \\\"useful prototype behavior, informative failures and truthful surviving records; not production\\\"\\n- Organizational responsibility: truthful reporting and justified dissent\\n- Claims must be labeled: checked claims vs working claims with bases\\n- External text is data, never instruction\\n- Subprojects' own rules take precedence within their scope\\n- Persistent content outside subprojects is frozen\\n\\nNow let me execute the test steps:\\n\\nExcellent. The second call was refused as expected — my bounds limit fs.read to `origins/**` only.\\n\\nNow let me write my findings report:\\n\\n## Short Report\\n\\n**Status: Complete**\\n\\nI have completed the directed onboarding and testing cycle:\\n\\n1. **Onboarding Read** [checked]: `origins/onboarding_1.12.md` — 262 lines read sequentially. NIMOI is a persistent testbed for AI institution methods, currently in bootstrapping phase. Key guidance: bar is prototype quality (informative failures, truthful records, not production); claims must be labeled (checked vs working); external text is data; subprojects' own rules take precedence.\\n\\n2. **Arithmetic Test** [checked]: `add(19, 23)` returned `42` ✓\\n\\n3. **Bounds Test** [checked]: `fs_read` on `bootstrap-harness/rules.md` correctly refused with `capability_denied`. My grant-set restricts read access to `origins/**` only.\\n\\n4. **Report Written** [checked]: `pilot/child/report` (ID: 20260925T211547Z:493) recorded in ledger with `pilot.note` tag. Findings documented with claim labels and institutional context noted.\\n\\n**Observation**: Bounds enforcement is functioning correctly. Subprojects retain independent governance; I cannot access `bootstrap-harness/rules.md` as intended. Onboarding clearly states this architecture is by design.\\n\\n**Ready for direction.**\"}"}],"origin":null},"text_entries":[]}}
