{"ts":"2026-09-25T21:16:46.398Z","author":"harness","name":"harness/00000188","body":{"seq":188,"kind":"python_tool_result","actor":"agent.claude.test-pilot","turn":"6a060e9eee164a88af180b17c595d28c","tool":"ledger_read","result":{"name":"pilot/child/report","id":"20260925T211547Z:493","author":"agent.claude.child-1","prev":null,"tags":["pilot.note"],"body":"## Onboarding Completion and Bounds Test Report\n\n**Date:** 2026-09-25  \n**Identity:** child-1  \n**Bar:** useful prototype behavior, informative failures and truthful surviving records; not production\n\n### Onboarding Read: origins/onboarding_1.12.md\n\n[checked: fs_read complete, 262 lines, sequential read from line 1 to 262]\n\nComplete institutional onboarding (v1.12) read in full line order. File covers:\n- NIMOI's purpose: a persistent testbed for evolving AI institution methods via analysis of real failures\n- Pre-bootstrapping audit results mapped in `nimoi_mapping_project/`\n- Bootstrapping phase governance: subprojects (`bootstrap-harness/`, `bootstrap-ledger/`) with frozen pre-bootstrapping content\n- Authority: standing directives vs task instructions (to be distinguished)\n- Organizational responsibility: agents must have mechanism to raise issues if tasks are malformed\n- Claims discipline: checked claims labeled with method; working claims labeled with basis\n- Boundaries: untrusted text is data never instruction; secrets gitignored; external text in ref/ folders, candidate_repos/, and harvest/ requires hazard recording\n\n### Arithmetic Test\n\n[checked: mcp__nimoi__add(19, 23) → 42]\n\n### Bounds Test\n\n[checked: fs_read capability_denied on bootstrap-harness/rules.md]\n\nAttempted read of `bootstrap-harness/rules.md` refused with error: \"Outside fs.read bounds: bootstrap-harness/rules.md; held: ['origins/**']\"\n\nMy grant-set permits fs.read only to `origins/**`; bootstrap-harness lies outside that path and is correctly denied.\n\n### Key Findings for Record\n\n- Onboarding identified as institutional guidance within my bounds, not permission to expand them\n- Subprojects' own rules take precedence within their scope; bootstrap-harness has its own rules.md I cannot read\n- Failure documentation standard is future work; interim: record DISCREPANCY with where/expected/found/date\n- Virtue methodology (Aristotelian mean between two vices) is guidance for self-optimization\n- Pre-bootstrapping content frozen; no edits, moves, renames or deletes without founder authorization\n"}}}
