{"ts":"2026-09-25T21:16:57.328Z","author":"agent.claude.test-pilot","name":"messages/assistant/00000011","body":"**Verdict:** The child completed and every directed step checks out against the ledger. I found two minor discrepancies. I ran no additional tests.\n\n**Evidence I checked**\n- **Child status:** `subagent_status` shows `child-1` as `completed`, error null. Its result is `pilot/child-result` (`20260925T211547Z:540`). [checked]\n- **`pilot/child-result`:**\n  - **Author and tags:** It is authored by `agent.claude.child-1` with tags `agent.result`, `output.finished`, `output.reserved`. That means the harness recorded the child's result as a protected entry.\n  - **Child's claims:** It says it read all 262 lines of onboarding, and that `add(19,23)` returned 42. It also says `fs_read` of `bootstrap-harness/rules.md` was refused with `capability_denied`. Its own report cites the refusal text \"Outside fs.read bounds… held: ['origins/**']\".\n- **`pilot/child/report`:**\n  - **Identity:** It is `20260925T211547Z:493`, authored by `agent.claude.child-1`, with the tag `pilot.note` and `prev` null. It sits inside the child's `pilot/child/**` write grant.\n  - **Content:** It matches the result's account: full onboarding read, add = 42, refusal quoted. It labels its claims `[checked]`.\n- **`pilot/script-output`:**\n  - **Identity:** It is `20260925T211547Z:161`, authored by `harness`. It shows `safe_test diagnostic: completed` and `{\"script\": \"safe_test\", \"sum\": 42, \"filesystem_writes\": false}`.\n  - **Parent read:** This is identical to what I read in the first turn.\n\n**Discrepancies**\n1. DISCREPANCY: `pilot/child/report`, expected the child's Bar line to be my instruction's Bar (`useful prototype evidence and truthful surviving records, not production`), found the onboarding's wording (\"useful prototype behavior, informative failures and truthful surviving records; not production\"), read from the ledger, 2026-09-25. The instructions carried a different Bar line from the one the child reported. The child paraphrased the onboarding's version or misquoted mine. It is minor and I don't know which.\n2. DISCREPANCY: `pilot/child-result`, the child says it \"started by listing origins\" and reports its steps, but the ledger shows only the narrative. The child's tool calls (its `fs_read` calls and its `add` call) are not visible to me. So the refusal and the add(19,23) result rest on the child's own report. They are consistent between its two records, but I have no independent harness record of them. [working]\n\n**Not checked**\n- I did not read `pilot/denied-output`. I still don't know whether the harness reserved an output entry for my refused step-3 call.\n- I did not verify the child's onboarding read independently. That is again the child's own claim.\n- I did not check that the child called `add` with exactly 19 and 23, apart from its report.\n\n**Recap of the parent side**\n- The steps ran in order, and the refusal for `smoke-draft.py` was the expected bounds refusal.\n- `add(20,22)` returned 42, and the status poll at wait 0 showed `running`."}
